cs.com\/epolls\/2016\/president\/ia\/iowa_trump_vs_clinton_vs_johnson_vs_stein-5981.html\">President<\/a>\u00a0|\u00a0<a href=\"http:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2016\/senate\/ia\/iowa_senate_grassley_vs_judge-5978.html\">Senate<\/a><span>\u00a0<\/span>|\u00a0<a href=\"http:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2016\/house\/ia\/iowa_1st_district_blum_vs_vernon-6038.html\">IA-1<\/a>,\u00a0<a href=\"http:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2016\/house\/ia\/iowa_3rd_district_young_vs_mowrer-6066.html\">IA-3<\/a><strong><br \/>2014<span>:\u00a0<\/span><\/strong><a href=\"http:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2014\/governor\/ia\/iowa_governor_branstad_vs_hatch-3647.html\">Governor<\/a>\u00a0|\u00a0<a href=\"http:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2014\/house\/ia\/iowa_1st_district_blum_vs_murphy-5073.html\">IA-1<\/a><span>\u00a0<\/span>|<span>\u00a0<\/span><a href=\"http:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2014\/house\/ia\/iowa_2nd_district_millermeeks_vs_loebsack-5076.html\">IA-2<\/a><span>\u00a0<\/span>|<span>\u00a0<\/span><a href=\"http:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2014\/house\/ia\/iowa_3rd_district_young_vs_appel-5125.html\">IA-3<\/a>\u00a0|<span>\u00a0<\/span><a href=\"http:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2014\/house\/ia\/iowa_4th_district_king_vs_mowrer-5223.html\">IA-4<\/a><strong><br \/><\/strong><\/p>"},"dataAnalysis":{"title":"Race Analysis","content":"<p>Iowa was initially one of the most heavily Republican states in the country. After George W. Jones left office in 1859, Iowa did not send another Democratic senator to Washington until Daniel Steck prevailed in the contested 1924 election. Until 1990, it had never elected a Democratic senator to two consecutive full terms. But the GOP\u2019s grip on Iowa began to weaken in the 1960s, when the state\u2019s dovish tendencies and history of support for social reform movements moved it toward the Democrats. After the 1974 elections, it had only one Republican congressman: Charles Grassley. Grassley won a Senate seat in 1980, defeating Sen. John Culver by a large margin; this followed Roger Jepsen\u2019s defeat of incumbent Democrat Dick Clark in 1978 and seemed to signal the beginning of a revival of Republican fortunes.<\/p>\n<p>But the farm crisis of the 1980s reversed this trend, and populist Democrat Tom Harkin, elected to the House the same year as Grassley, defeated Jepsen by a surprisingly large margin. Harkin retired in 2014 and was replaced by Joni Ernst, who is retiring this year.<\/p>\n<p>Iowa shifted right again in the late 2010s and early 2020s. Donald Trump won the state handily in 2016, 2020, and 2024; Ernst won re-election in 2020 by six points.\u00a0Republicans now hold hefty majorities in both chambers of the legislature.\u00a0But a seemingly unfavorable Republican environment, combined with anger in farm states over tariffs, gives Democrats a realistic shot at winning the seat. Republicans have a charismatic candidate in Rep. Ashley Hinson. Democrats, however, have state Rep. Josh Turek, a wheelchair basketball player with a compelling story. This looks like a close race for now.<\/p>"},"showLineChart":1,"showBarChart":1,"showLineChartFirst":0,"sideCharts":{"charts_on_top":0,"left_chart_race_id":"7072","right_chart_race_id":"3990"},"show_final_results":0,"chart_data":{"chart_id":"7487","chart_axis_x":"1","chart_grid_x":"4","chart_axis_y":"1","chart_grid_y":"10","chart_min":"","chart_max":"","chart_start":"1775883600","chart_end":"","poll_id":"8930","chart_highlight":"#bbbb00","chart_days_extend":"7","chart_height":"360","chart_height_mobile":"360","chart_html5":"1","chart_main_percent":"70","chart_spread_percent":"30","chart_spread_range":"10","chart_name_in_tooltips":"1","chart_spread_force_0_y_axis":"1","chart_y_axis_min":"42","chart_y_axis_max":"50","chart_y_axis_min_m":"42","chart_y_axis_max_m":"50","chart_dates":{"7D":"0","14D":"0","30D":"0","MAX":"1"},"chart_dates_old":[{"period":"DD","count":"14","label":"